Make "audio telepathy" into sonar, a la the character "Dare Devil" in
Spiderman.  Make telekinesis line-of-sight; it lets you move an object one
space per turn (heavy things, like boulders) or faster, for lighter
objects.  Change "control" to "extension" - you can do it
non-line-of-sight.  You need to handcuff yourself to do it, though.  (Just
like blindfolds - we have handcuffs.  Also useful on nymphs!  :-) )

>Maybe these intrinsics would make the player too powerful;  
>perhaps make tk/tkc incompatible with teleport/tpc (this
>would give those particular rings a lot more power though).

No incompatibility; it's a bad idea.  That'd be like having cold and heat
resistance mutually exclusive - a bug if ever I heard of one.  Telekinesis
extension should be really hard to get.

Eating a giant bat (instead of stunning you; that's stupid; how does
eating bat stun you?) should give you a 1% chance (cumulative) of getting
sonar.  Since it's not magical, wand of cancellation does not kill it.

>Also definitely have monsters with these intrinsics; make it
>not incompatible for them and make some obscure way for 
>players to overcome the incompatibility ie polymorph and
>eat all the rings.

Create a new class - esper.  Espers start with telepathy, telekinesis,
(but not extension) and gain x-ray vision, polymorph and control, teleport
and control, and telekinesis extension at different levels.  (The
"controls" should be the last ones to get; simulates the "uncontrollable"
peroid of developing psi powers.

Give alignment a little change - use the full 2-d matrix.  (Lawful,
neutral, chaotic; good, neutral, evil.)  Lawful-chaotic controls if you
can steal or not; good-evil controls whether you can do nasty things like
cannibalism, human sacrifice, etc.  In addition, evil gods are more
uncontrollable (add a random factor to luck).  If you "stray"
sufficiently, you should change alignment automatically, at a luck loss.

