Cliffs and lofts are good things; let you see into the next level. 
Forests would have to be mushroom forests and fungal jungles, tended by
shadow elves or dwerro or some such.  Elevators good; swarms bad.  (There
already are beehives, you know.)  More multi-space monsters - dragons are
a LOT bigger than humans!

More variety in monsters.  Pull out your Monster Manuals, Fiend Folio, and
Creature Catalogue.  Dump 'em all in.  Agarats, fungoids, nupperibos,
neo-otyughs and otyughs; meenlocks, everything.  The works.  Throw in a
few minor demon princes (make 'em pit fiends) and higher-order Archons. 
Add more "heavenly" and "hellish" beings, from other planes.  Modrons! 
Slaad!  The works.  (I'd love to see a Wizard try to fight a swarm of
monodrones.)  Hell should be full of larvae and nupperibos.  Add githyanki
and githzerai, and of course a decent (infinite, or close to it) astral
plane.  Add ethereal travel, more summonation spells, and gating.  Add a
resurrect spell for pets; a reality-shift, in case you mess up your quest
severely.  Greater bless/curse range; since we're using the full alignment
matrix, invent something like bless/curse for lawful/chaotic, since
"bless/curse" is for good/evil.  Make cursed items work well for evils;
blessed ones act "cursed" to them.  Call the new things "entropize" and
"energize" or some thermodynamic type name.  Entropic things work well for
chaotics, of course.

